    {
      "pointer": "/wholeCurrentOperativeCasesAndAuthoredReferenceResponses/0/wholeOperativeCase/expectedAnswer/en",
      "before": "An acceptable plan uses equal 10.00-mL aliquots, standardised base, clean prepared instruments, an endpoint suitable for a weak acid and repeated volumes. Reference: 8.00 mL for A and 16.00 mL for B yield cA = 0.00800 mol/L, cB = 0.0160 mol/L and ratio 2.00. Actual execution and own raw values must be independently recorded. pH alone does not prove a concentration ratio of 2 because of dissociation equilibrium; an appropriate amount analysis can within its uncertainty. Indicator choice uses the stated transition range and own curve: methyl orange changes before the alkaline equivalence region in this weak-acid titration; phenolphthalein requires a controlled first faint colour change and assessment of endpoint bias. Actually log calibration with current buffers; their nominal values are not sample readings.",
      "after": "An acceptable plan uses equal 10.00-mL aliquots, standardised base, clean prepared instruments, an endpoint suitable for a weak acid and repeated volumes. Reference: 8.00 mL for A and 16.00 mL for B yield cA = 0.00800 mol/L, cB = 0.0160 mol/L and concentration ratio cB/cA = 2.00. Actual execution and own raw values must be independently recorded. pH alone does not prove a concentration ratio of 2 because of dissociation equilibrium; an appropriate amount analysis can within its uncertainty. Indicator choice uses the stated transition range and own curve: methyl orange changes before the alkaline equivalence region in this weak-acid titration; phenolphthalein requires a controlled first faint colour change and assessment of endpoint bias. Actually log calibration with current buffers; their nominal values are not sample readings."
